WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.060
OK.

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:04.970
Let's get into audience questions for the
week, a lot of very similar, it's clear what

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.549
the audience is thinking about and I understand
why.

00:00:07.549 --> 00:00:14.560
First question is, David, what do we do if
Donald Trump refuses to accept election results?

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:18.949
So there's two different ways that accept
can be interpreted.

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:24.590
He refuses to accept them and that he claims
it was rigged, but he's still leaving or he

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.499
refuses to accept it and that he's going to
try to stay in the White House.

00:00:28.499 --> 00:00:35.080
Now, I want to again restate, most likely
we don't have to do anything because Donald

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.980
Trump, if he loses in November, come January
21st, will simply not be the president.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:43.040
He's just not the president anymore.

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.100
Now, for me, the biggest concern is trump
rigging the election and winning that.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.660
I think that's a bigger concern than him not
accepting the results.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:54.660
But let's play it out.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.910
We see Trump undermined democracy.

00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:00.780
He jokes about staying in power a long time.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:05.649
He says to Chris Wallace on Sunday, this past
Sunday, he's not yet ready to commit to accepting

00:01:05.649 --> 00:01:06.860
the results.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.109
So now there are articles being published
about what what we would have to do if that

00:01:11.109 --> 00:01:12.409
was the case.

00:01:12.409 --> 00:01:15.750
And most of them say, well, we would have
to mobilize.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:18.979
Listen, you and I aren't removing Donald Trump.

00:01:18.979 --> 00:01:22.259
It's ultimately going to depend on the systems
that we have.

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:27.359
So from a practical standpoint, the most likely
scenario is Trump is going to leave because

00:01:27.359 --> 00:01:30.299
on January 21st, he would not be president
anymore.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:33.789
If he loses the November election and there
would be a new president and at that point

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:37.689
he would be trespassing in the Oval Office
and he would be escorted out.

00:01:37.689 --> 00:01:42.350
But where I believe our efforts are better
spent because we ultimately can't control

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.350
that.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:48.229
And I do trust that he will will be removed
if he physically tried to stay.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:54.340
What we can do is it's only July, so we're
better off doing what we can do to prevent

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:00.319
vote rigging, making sure people aren't dropped
from voter rolls and fighting that in court

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:03.689
as has been done, expanding absentee ballot
access.

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:09.270
I just filled out my absentee ballot application
this week and planned to vote by by mail,

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:13.280
all of that stuff, because with all of these
things and this is going to come up again

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.680
later in the segment, prevention is cheaper
than the cure.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:23.260
If Trump tries to stay in office, I really
don't know how he gets away with it.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.880
He won't be president anymore.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:29.630
Somebody else will be smoke sworn in and eventually
he's going to be removed and he's not going

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:30.630
to be.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.740
The president made that naive.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.740
Right.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:37.129
I mean, it's like are there people listening
who really think that that's naive, that even

00:02:37.129 --> 00:02:42.340
something like that, like if Biden wins and
he shows up ready for work with his lunchbox

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:46.650
and everything and trumps there and he says,
I'm not leaving, that that's going to be allowed

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:47.650
to happen.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.159
I don't believe that that's going to be allowed
to happen.

00:02:50.159 --> 00:02:54.150
If you believe I'm wrong, I want to hear what
the path would be.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:58.510
And I understand the fear, which is Trump
has flouted every norm.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:04.250
He's, you know, constitutional violations,
emoluments, all of this difference of I get

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.250
it.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:08.750
I still don't think that he is going to be
able to stay.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:14.159
I actually think that Trump the narcissist,
if he loses and this is a big if and we don't

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:16.870
want to put the cart before the horse and
we've got a vote and all of that that I've

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:23.469
been saying, I think if Trump loses, his narcissism
will force him to essentially say, I didn't

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:30.209
want it any way to essentially make it undesirable
when when you have an extreme narcissist and

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:34.810
you take away from them something that they
want, what they typically do is they say,

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:39.219
I didn't really want it or I don't want it
anymore or it's not worth that much anymore.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.219
Let someone else have it.

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:43.450
I'll make more money in real estate, et cetera.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:47.280
So that is more likely to me if Trump loses
to basically say.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:48.340
I'm out.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:51.739
You know, I'm better off going back to real
estate.

00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:56.700
Good luck with Joe Biden or whatever, then
trying to stay in power, because that's often

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.280
how the narcissist works.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.989
Now, the authoritarian narcissist may try
to stay in power.

00:04:02.989 --> 00:04:07.319
And Trump certainly has no shortage of authoritarian
tendencies.

00:04:07.319 --> 00:04:09.690
But I believe if he loses, he will leave.

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:14.030
Let's focus on preventing the election from
being rigged against Biden.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:05:48.089
There we can do something.

